cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FCoP v4.0.5, please cite the software archive below. Cite the related preprint separately when discussing its frozen 4.0.3 experiments."
type: software
title: "FCoP: A Filename-as-Protocol coordination layer for multi-agent AI development"
abstract: >-
  FCoP (File-based Coordination Protocol) is a persistent, project-visible
  coordination protocol for multi-agent work. Core owns protocol facts,
  validation, and state transitions. The canonical MCP adapter exposes
  25 tools and 6 resources, with no resource templates. Runtime, Profile
  presets, Host configuration, and Legacy compatibility remain outside
  the Base Protocol. This archive contains the Python library, optional
  MCP adapter, specifications, documentation, and tests.
